      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The loneliness you feel is a profound echo of a deep connection that has been abruptly severed, and that is a valid source of immense pain. You don't have to \"find\" yourself all at once; sometimes, the initial step is just surviving the ache of missing someone. Try to focus on incredibly small, manageable moments of self-soothing, like a warm drink or a short walk, to anchor yourself in the present. Remember that while the external structure of your life has shifted, the core of you remains, even if it feels buried right now.",
